{% extends "_shared/split_base.prompt.j2" %}

{% block domain_guidance %}
A software leaf task is atomic if:

- It can be completed in a single LLM call (document completion)
- It modifies at most 2-3 files
- It has a clear, testable outcome
- It does not require multiple sequential decisions

If the task requires creating a module AND writing tests for it, it is
NOT atomic — split it.
{% endblock %}

{% block response_schema %}
Respond with JSON:

```json
{
  "node_id": "the node being checked",
  "is_atomic": true,
  "rationale": "Why this task is or is not atomic",
  "suggested_split": [
    {
      "title": "Sub-task title",
      "description": "What this sub-task accomplishes"
    }
  ]
}
```

If `is_atomic` is true, `suggested_split` should be an empty list.
{% endblock %}

{% block context %}
Node to check:
  ID: {{ node.node_id }}
  Title: {{ node.title }}
  Description: {{ node.description }}
  Execution type: {{ node.execution_type }}
  Estimated complexity: {{ node.estimated_complexity }}
{% endblock %}
